            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for the separation, then the Portuguese for the move."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: o falecimento",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "o falecimento — \"the passing, the death (formal)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "O falecimento do avô juntou a família toda. Grandfather’s passing brought the whole family together."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A respectful word, common in notices."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "falecimento is built on falecer \"to pass away\", with the ending -mento; the verb goes back to Vulgar Latin fallēscere (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
